  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14197487/assets/393c612a7ecb682e28bf9de46024a3681e8f6e58a9add78c0b24a870aa00fa7a.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[0,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $8.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0,4]$ given that $f(0)=-1.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
